 "text": "You're getting better you just can't see it. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 29. Tara sang 20 minutes a day for two months. Every day sounded like yesterday. So she decided she wasn't good at it and almost quit. The catch you compare today with yesterday and one day of practice is too small to hear. The change only shows across weeks. So every Sunday Tara recorded the same minute of the same song and never deleted one. Running same two kilometers timed, riding same prompt 10 minutes. In week 8 she played week 1 then week 8. Two months of progress she couldn't hear all at once. Send this to someone who thinks they've stopped improving. That's what Demure is for. Archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day, next, why telling people your goal makes it harder. What would you record every Sunday? The link's in the bio.",
